  "text.aa4b3f0491fc": "Three questions that come up every summer — why carbon peels get booked before events, whether massage does anything beyond feeling nice, and how a lash lift holds up in humidity.",
  "text.aaeaabe57c0b": "Before you book",
  "text.ab80cec9380f": "Plan to discuss your goals, relevant health and treatment history, current routine, and questions. Your provider will explain suitable options, tradeoffs, expected results, aftercare, and pricing before you decide.",
  "text.ab92cd840a38": "Three to six sessions, spaced every two to four weeks, is the range Anima publishes. The number that suits you is confirmed with your provider.",
  "text.abb81f03208a": "Source image published on Anima’s current Signature Facial page.",
  "text.ac3a5f8f9428": "Skin changes with more than the seasons. A case for steady, unhurried care rather than a correction every few months.",
  "text.ace13fdfb6b3": "On average, men produce more sebum than women, have thicker skin, and have larger pores. Anyone who shaves is also putting the barrier through daily mechanical exfoliation. None of that is a complaint — it is simply biology, and it changes what summer does.",
  "text.ad04e4c00a99": "Clients consistently highlight friendly, professional service and attentive care. Read the original reviews before choosing what feels right for you.",
